QcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"580fdd64f3d5adde54706fede643cf471775eb6ead44036269efe6ba711acfba","event_uuid":"162644c8-a47f-474a-9042-499818ba3040","position":{"commit_sha":"df7e4f9518bd7222609ed98c36ed06376c21d0b4","position":"1787072824674847001-162644c8-a47f-474a-9042-499818ba3040"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## AWAITING USER DECISION — pydantic-ai v2 OpenAI API semantics\n\nEvidence: current tests exercise custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints through `infer_model` and pydantic-ai warns that the existing `openai:` prefix will change meaning in v2 from Chat Completions to Responses. Choosing a replacement prefix is behavioral, not a mechanical deprecation cleanup.\n\n**A — Preserve Chat Completions (recommended):** change rebar-owned model construction to `openai-chat:`. This preserves today's wire protocol and broad custom-endpoint compatibility; held-out provider-parity tests must prove no outbound payload change.\n\n**B — Migrate to Responses:** use `openai-responses:` and intentionally adopt the newer API. This may change payloads, structured-output behavior, streaming, and endpoint compatibility; it requires explicit parity evidence and migration documentation.\n\n**C — Defer with a dependency bound:** retain `openai:` and pin pydantic-ai below v2 temporarily. This avoids an immediate behavior choice but carries upgrade debt and leaves the warning unresolved.\n\nRecommendation: approve A unless there is a product goal to adopt Responses now. No code, claim, or implementation work will begin until the user selects the intended behavior.","timestamp":1786914967354109001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Decision (2026-08-17): preserve the existing Chat Completions semantics during the pydantic-ai v2 compatibility repair by using the explicit `openai-chat:` prefix. The user approved this compatibility-preserving choice and requested a separate story for the eventual deliberate migration to `openai-responses:`.","timestamp":1787017351072818001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA (confirmed before repair): `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py` maps inferred provider `openai` to the ambiguous pydantic-ai target `openai:` and returns explicitly qualified `openai:` model strings verbatim; `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py::_resolve_target` independently composes the same ambiguous qualifier for class and fallback targets. At runtime, pydantic-ai 1.107.2 `infer_model` parses that provider name and emits `PydanticAIDeprecationWarning` because v2 will reinterpret it as Responses. With that warning promoted to an error, five real OpenAI-compatible provider tests fail at `runner.py:390` or their real-seam helper; the exact same construction with `openai-chat:` creates `OpenAIChatModel` without the warning, ruling out provider construction and test filtering as causes. Compatibility companion: current `ProviderSession` keys both its cfg.base_url builder registration and its per-candidate endpoint-override guard only on `openai`; a direct `openai-chat:` experiment therefore built the stock provider at `https://api.openai.com/v1` instead of the configured loopback endpoint. Both gates must recognize the explicit qualifier or the warning fix would regress endpoint routing/profile behavior. Defect legitimacy: the operator explicitly approved preserving existing Chat Completions semantics and upstream names `openai-chat:` as that stable contract; future Responses migration is separately tracked by `upbeat-illadvised-springtail`. Caller sweep: `_pai_model`, `_resolve_target`, fallback construction, runner/provider session, capability lookup, pricing qualifier stripping, docs, and eval specs were inspected. Capability and qualifier consumers already recognize `openai-chat`; only the two ProviderSession gates behaviorally depend on the old bare name and are included in repair. No other provider target is to change.","timestamp":1787026979024866001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 2 blind-fixer implementation evidence (held-out validation still pending investigator):\n\n- Primary inference and legacy-explicit `openai:` targets now normalize to `openai-chat:` in `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py`; non-OpenAI qualifiers remain unchanged.\n- Model-class primaries and fallbacks now normalize inferred, configured, and legacy-explicit OpenAI targets to `openai-chat:` in `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py`, while treating `openai` and `openai-chat` as compatible spellings for conflict detection.\n- `ProviderSession` registers and selects the custom-endpoint builder for `openai-chat` as well as the legacy alias, preserving endpoint injection and the surgical structured-output profile override.\n- User-facing examples in the three scoped LLM/workflow docs now recommend `openai-chat:`. Visible contract assertions were updated for primary, explicit, class, fallback, interface, hosted, missing-extra, and custom-endpoint behavior.\n- Verification: 193 focused visible tests passed across `test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`, `test_openai_compatible_provider.py`, `test_provider_qualifier.py`, `test_llm_provider_factory.py`, `test_model_classes.py`, and `tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py`. The real loopback provider tests remained green and emitted no `PydanticAIDeprecationWarning` (one unrelated pydantic-ai event-loop `DeprecationWarning` remains). `make lint` passed, including complexity/doc/workflow gates. `make typecheck` passed: 555 source files, no issues. `git diff --check` passed.\n- Safety: this restores the operator-approved Chat Completions contract, adds no dependency, preserves other providers, and weakens no test. No commit or push was made. I did not inspect, seek, or recreate the removed warning-as-error held-out oracle. Final held-out GREEN, defect-seeded mutation RED, and acceptance disposition remain with the investigator/orchestrator.","timestamp":1787027319915250001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"rebar-debug final repair report.\n\nProblem: rebar emitted ambiguous `openai:` Pydantic-AI model targets; Pydantic AI 1.107.2 warns that v2 changes that prefix from Chat Completions to Responses.\n\nProven root cause/proof: `_pai_model` and model-class `_resolve_target` preserved/emitted `openai:`. Runtime `infer_model` under warning-as-error produced `PydanticAIDeprecationWarning`; replacing the target with `openai-chat:` constructed `OpenAIChatModel` without warning. The cfg.base_url builder-registration and per-candidate endpoint-override gates also matched only the legacy provider name, so the explicit target needed parity there.\n\nTest: the final held-out oracle in `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py` covered inferred `gpt-4o` + provider `openai`, legacy explicit `openai:gpt-4o`, and model-class target resolution. It was RED first (3 failures), was absent from the blind fixer’s worktree, then GREEN. Reintroducing the exact old `openai:` output in both production seams returned all three cases to RED (two deprecation failures plus the target assertion); restoring the fix returned them to GREEN.\n\nFix: inferred and legacy-explicit OpenAI targets normalize to `openai-chat:` across primary, model-class, and fallback resolution; custom base URL and per-candidate endpoint builders accept that explicit qualifier; documentation examples now recommend it. Other provider targets are unchanged. This implements the user-approved Chat Completions contract.\n\nScope/safety: caller sweep covered direct runner resolution, model-class/fallback composition, cfg.base_url, and candidate endpoint override. The change freezes existing wire semantics, creates no new capability or dependency, and weakens no test. Provider/warning matrix: 244 passed with `PydanticAIDeprecationWarning` promoted to error. Original provider reproduction: 13 passed with that warning promoted to error. Broader unit/interface sweep, lint, typecheck, complexity, formatting, and diff checks pass.\n\nSiblings/parity: all live target-construction seams were normalized. Current eval-spec grader `openai:` strings are report-only: `run_eval` executes deterministic scorers and does not construct those models, so they are not live siblings. CLI/library/workflow callers converge on the repaired shared resolver/session.\n\nResidual risk/prevention: migration to OpenAI Responses is intentionally out of scope and tracked by `upbeat-illadvised-springtail` (`155c-218b-c128-4700`), per user approval. Report-only eval grader strings remain accepted as inert metadata until that story owns migration.\n\nReplication: both inferred and legacy-explicit OpenAI paths now build `OpenAIChatModel` through the real Pydantic-AI inference boundary without the announced-v2 deprecation.","timestamp":1787029509962743001}],"created_at":1786914866214820001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"722a94a9-a1e5-4786-848b-8b0057d725e4","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0024-fa99-d5bb-49bc"},{"link_uuid":"507955aa-0a11-4274-87a2-a774e318b49d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9c72-c44a-3421-45ad"},{"link_uuid":"91612633-a063-4bf2-b481-22933feb482b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8d53-4d0f-3