canonical examples for ambiguous `openai:` spellings while excluding intentional legacy-compatibility tests ...\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Inferred OpenAI targets resolve to `openai-chat:`; verified by provider-resolution tests.\n- [x] Legacy-explicit `openai:` targets resolve to `openai-chat:`; verified by interface tests.\n- [x] Primary and fallback model-class targets resolve to `openai-chat:`; verified by model-class tests.\n- [x] Configured `openai`/`openai-chat` and inline `openai:`/`openai-chat:` are treated as one provider family and ca...\n- [x] Cross-family provider conflicts and non-OpenAI target behavior remain unchanged.\n- [x] Real model construction emits no `pydantic_ai._warnings.PydanticAIDeprecationWarning` with that exact category ...\n- [x] Loopback custom endpoints still receive Chat Completions payloads; verified by real-seam provider tests.\n- [x] The custom-endpoint profile override remains active on cfg.base_url and per-candidate endpoint paths.\n- [x] Canonical operator/developer examples and provider-matrix contracts use `openai-chat:` for Chat Completions.\n- [x] Description-only schema changes have deliberately refreshed golden hashes.\n- [x] Focused tests pass.\n- [x] Repository lint passes.\n- [x] Repository typecheck passes.\n[full output: \"$HOME/Library/Application Support/rtk/tee/1787072235_jq_-r__description.log\"]","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py","reason":"normalize primary OpenAI Pydantic AI targets to explicit Chat Completions"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py","reason":"normalize model-class and fallback OpenAI targets"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/providers.py","reason":"register both custom-endpoint gates for explicit openai-chat qualifier"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py","reason":"held-out warning-as-error oracle and inferred/explicit resolution contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_openai_compatible_provider.py","reason":"warnin